      "textEn": "He is not actually free from the fruits of sinful deeds, but if he chants the holy name of God,\nthen with just a shadow of such chanting, he is immediately freed from all sins. The glory of the Lord's name, the chanting of it, brings forth all good fortune. Therefore, there is no doubt\nthat Ajamila should not be punished by Yamraj because of being completely free from the fruits of all sins.\"\n\nWhen they were saying this, the messengers of Vishnu freed Ajamila from the noose of the messengers of Yama, and they\nwent to their abode. But the Brahmin Ajamila paid reverence to the Vishnu messengers. Then,\nHe understood how fortunate he was that at the end of his life, he uttered the name of Narayan. Undoubtedly, he could experience the full importance of his good fortune. After thoroughly understanding the debate between the messengers of Yama and the messengers of Vishnu, he became a pure devotee of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. He greatly repented that how big a sinner he was.\nAnd repeatedly blamed himself.\nFinally, upon awakening from his original consciousness through the association of Vishnu's messengers, Ajamila gave up everything.\nAnd went to Haridwar, where he, with unwavering devotion, began to contemplate the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Then Vishnuduta arrived there and he seated him on the golden throne.\nAnd then he took him to Vaikuntha Loka. In short, although sinful Ajamila called out to his son, Narayan's holy name,\neven when uttered in the initial state (Namabhas), could bring him salvation. Therefore, the person who\npronounces the holy name of God with faith and devotion is definitely great,\nand his protection is also done in his physical bound life. Sribadarayaniruvacha"
